From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <zenithblue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:04:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: flush the transient pool BO only up to
 transient_offset

Rationale: panvk_pool_flush_maps() cleaned every WB-mapped pool BO in
full, including the unused tail of the current transient slab (perf
review 2026-10-22, "Flushing" in the submit notes).
Expected gain: CPU at vkEndCommandBuffer and JM re-submit. A command
buffer that uses a few KiB of a 64 KiB desc/cs slab now cleans only
those lines: up to about 60 KiB less cache maintenance per pool per
flush, more for small command buffers.

The transient BO is used only below transient_offset (rounded up to a
64-byte line). The other BOs have no used-size record and are still
cleaned whole. Pools without WB_MMAP return early, as before.

Knob: PANVK_POOL_FLUSH_FULL=1 restores the full flush.
Arch: all (common code). Not device-tested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Purpose: M5 (221): CPU at vkEndCommandBuffer: panvk_pool_flush_maps() cleans the current transient BO only up to transient_offset (64-byte aligned) instead of the whole slab (up to ~60 KiB less cache clean per 64 KiB slab); other BOs still flushed in full. PANVK_POOL_FLUSH_FULL=1 reverts
Upstream-commit: zenithblue csf-v11/221 (port)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: none; applies on the full g615-v11-csf series after rg477m/030 (git am of csf-v11/221, clean)
Validation test: built OK at this commit on memport (bld.sh, 0 new warnings) and at next tip 7390330e in compat and unsafe; combined build next.so (15c3385bbe40, rg477m/023-037): PanProbe 38/38 x2 (unsafe profile 37/38, only the bc_decode raw readback, by design); 16-game boot sweep 2026-10-25 in quietd Stock mode: Hades 60, Jupiter Hell 59, Risk of Rain 2 38, Moonlighter 60, Megabonk 60, Portal 2 60, Gladius 60, Crysis 3 Remastered 60 fps; Arkham Asylum to the menu; Factorio and Ashes menus render as before; Descenders, Tomb Raider, Doom 3 BFG and Metro 2033 match their known states; 0 GPU faults; Serious Sam bot benchmark A-B-B-A compat 49.2/52.7 vs next 53.3/51.1 fps; Arkham Asylum 20-round interleaved A/B 2026-10-25 (quietd Stock), base rg477m vs next: launch failures 1/20 vs 0/20 (session total 1/33 vs 4/36, not significant; B5 signatures also seen on the stock driver), gameplay fps median 36.4 vs 36.5, speckcount on 3 gameplay frames per run 0-1 px in both arms (base 2 runs with 1 px, next 3 runs with 1 px; the old specks bug gave tens to hundreds): no specks; Arkham gameplay specks check (cache maintenance, cf. rg477m/021): no specks in the 20-round A/B above (PANVK_POOL_FLUSH_FULL=1 remains the switch for a dedicated A/B)
Channel: compatibility, unsafe
Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_mempool.c | 28 ++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_mempool.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_mempool.c
index 6e4411f6..41b5057b 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_mempool.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_mempool.c
@@ -280,11 +280,31 @@ panvk_pool_flush_maps(struct panvk_pool *pool)
    if (!(pool->props.create_flags & PAN_KMOD_BO_FLAG_WB_MMAP))
       return;
 
-   list_for_each_entry(struct panvk_priv_bo, bo, &pool->bos, node)
-      panvk_priv_bo_flush(bo, 0, bo->bo->size);
+   /* csf-v11 221: the transient BO is used only up to transient_offset,
+    * so its unused tail is not flushed. Other BOs have no used-size record
+    * and are flushed whole. PANVK_POOL_FLUSH_FULL=1 flushes everything.
+    */
+   static int full = -1;
+   if (full < 0) {
+      const char *e = getenv("PANVK_POOL_FLUSH_FULL");
+      full = e && e[0] == '1';
+   }
 
-   list_for_each_entry(struct panvk_priv_bo, bo, &pool->big_bos, node)
-      panvk_priv_bo_flush(bo, 0, bo->bo->size);
+   list_for_each_entry(struct panvk_priv_bo, bo, &pool->bos, node) {
+      size_t size = bo->bo->size;
+      if (!full && bo == pool->transient_bo)
+         size = MIN2(ALIGN_POT((size_t)pool->transient_offset, 64), size);
+      if (size)
+         panvk_priv_bo_flush(bo, 0, size);
+   }
+
+   list_for_each_entry(struct panvk_priv_bo, bo, &pool->big_bos, node) {
+      size_t size = bo->bo->size;
+      if (!full && bo == pool->transient_bo)
+         size = MIN2(ALIGN_POT((size_t)pool->transient_offset, 64), size);
+      if (size)
+         panvk_priv_bo_flush(bo, 0, size);
+   }
 }
 
 void
